sequence01	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	938060	938944	.	+	0	ID=MGA_862;product=type II secretion system F family protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_011269003.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_08600;note=WP_011269003.1 type II secretion system F family protein (Pseudomonas syringae) [pid:74.5%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:1.0e-119],Domain:cl19503:T2SSF Type II secretion system (T2SS)%2C protein F. The original family covered both the regions found by the current model. The splitting of the family has allowed the related FlaJ_arch (archaeal FlaJ family) to be merged with it. Proteins with this domain in form a platform for the machiney of the Type II secretion system%2C as well as the Type 4 pili and the archaeal flagella. This domain seems to show some similarity to PF00664 but this may just be due to similarities in the TM helices (personal obs: C Yeats). [Superfamily%2C Aligned:5-293%2C Eval:5.8e-48%2C score:159.8],MGA_862
