sequence01	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	1187266	1187661	.	-	0	ID=MGA_1068;product=hotdog domain-containing protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_002551711.1;translation=MNFHTRKWVKPEDLNPNGTLFGGSLLRWIDEEAAIYAIVQLGNQRVVTKYISEINFVSASRQGDIIELGITATEFGRTSITLKCQVRNKITRKSILTVEKIVFVNLDEDGQPAPHGRTEIRYIKDQFDVED;locus_tag=LOCUS_10660;note=WP_002551711.1 hotdog domain-containing protein (Pseudomonas) [pid:100.0%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:5.2e-71],Domain:cl00509:hot_dog N/A. This is the dehydratase domain of polyketide synthases. Structural analysis shows these DH domains are double hotdogs in which the active site contains a histidine from the N-terminal hotdog and an aspartate from the C-terminal hotdog. Studies have uncovered that a substrate tunnel formed between the DH domains may be essential for loading substrates and unloading products. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:5-114%2C Eval:5.4e-38%2C score:123.5],MGA_1068
