sequence01	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	1628969	1630705	.	+	0	ID=MGA_1480;product=OPT family oligopeptide transporter;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_005768135.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_14780;note=WP_005768135.1 OPT family oligopeptide transporter (Pseudomonas syringae group) [pid:89.8%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:5.4e-300],Domain:cl14607:OPT OPT oligopeptide transporter protein. This protein represents a small family of integral membrane proteins from Gram-negative bacteria%2C a Gram-positive bacteria%2C and an archaeal species. Members of this family contain 15 to 18 GES predicted transmembrane regions%2C and this family has extensive homology to a family of yeast tetrapeptide transporters%2C including isp4 (Schizosaccharomyces pombe) and Opt1 (Candida albicans). EspB%2C an apparent equivalog from Myxococcus xanthus%2C shares an operon with a two component system regulatory protein%2C and is required for the normal timing of sporulation after the aggregation of cells. This is consistent with a role in transporting oligopeptides as signals across the membrane. [Transport and binding proteins%2C Amino acids%2C peptides and amines] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:14-567%2C Eval:1.5e-31%2C score:126.3],MGA_1480
