sequence01	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	1785782	1786993	.	+	0	ID=MGA_1618;product=YeeE/YedE family protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_005768334.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_16160;note=WP_005768334.1 YeeE/YedE family protein (Pseudomonas syringae group) [pid:82.1%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:2.2e-190],Domain:cl19477:Sulf_transp Sulphur transport. For 79 of the first 80 reference genomes in which a member of this protein family%2C YedE%2C is found%2C a selenium utilization system is found%2C spread over a broad taxonomic range (Firmicutes%2C spirochetes%2C delta-proteobacteria%2C Fusobacteria%2C Bacteriodes%2C etc. This family is less widespread than YedF%2C also involved in selenium metabolism. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:38-181%2C Eval:9.9e-08%2C score:49.0],MGA_1618
sequence01	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	1787113	1788000	.	+	0	ID=MGA_1619;product=bestrophin family ion channel;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_003316074.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_16170;note=WP_003316074.1 bestrophin family ion channel (Pseudomonas) [pid:91.9%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:3.0e-156],Domain:cl01544:Bestrophin Bestrophin%2C RFP-TM%2C chloride channel. Bestrophin is a 68-kDa basolateral plasma membrane protein expressed in retinal pigment epithelial cells (RPE). It is encoded by the VMD2 gene%2C which is mutated in Best macular dystrophy%2C a disease characterized by a depressed light peak in the electrooculogram. VMD2 encodes a 585-amino acid protein with an approximate mass of 68 kDa which has been designated bestrophin. Bestrophin shares homology with the Caenorhabditis elegans RFP gene family%2C named for the presence of a conserved arginine (R)%2C phenylalanine (F)%2C proline (P)%2C amino acid sequence motif. Bestrophin is a plasma membrane protein%2C localized to the basolateral surface of RPE cells consistent with a role for bestrophin in the generation or regulation of the EOG light peak. Bestrophin and other RFP family members represent a new class of chloride channels%2C indicating a direct role for bestrophin in generating the light peak. The VMD2 gene underlying Best disease was shown to represent the first human member of the RFP-TM protein family. More than 97%25 of the disease-causing mutations are located in the N-terminal RFP-TM domain implying important functional properties. The bestrophins are four-pass transmembrane chloride-channel proteins%2C and the RFP-TM or bestrophin domain extends from the N-terminus through approximately 350 amino acids and contains all of the TM domains as well as nearly all reported disease causing mutations. Interestingly%2C the RFP motif is not conserved evolutionarily back beyond Metazoa%2C neither is it in plant members. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:13-285%2C Eval:8.9e-60%2C score:190.4],MGA_1619
