sequence02	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	73784	74218	.	+	0	ID=MGA_1726;product=prepilin-type N-terminal cleavage/methylation domain-containing protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_007246056.1;translation=MKASVASRGFTLMEMLVVLVLMSIAVGLVGFGLQQGLSTASERRAVGDMVEALRATRVRAIVTGQPARTEFNLRKATFKAPGKREMRWPVTLRVTLQTSSDLGSSVEFYPDGGSSGGNVLVADGDRRWRIDIGWLTGSVQVRSL;locus_tag=LOCUS_17240;note=WP_007246056.1 prepilin-type N-terminal cleavage/methylation domain-containing protein (Pseudomonas syringae group) [pid:88.2%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:1.2e-66],Domain:cl26823:N_methyl Prokaryotic N-terminal methylation motif. This model describes many but not all examples of the N-terminal region of bacterial proteins that resemble type IV pilins at their N-terminus%2C with a cleavage site G^FxxxE followed by a hydrophobic stretch. The new N-terminal residue%2C usually Phe%2C is methylated. Separate domains of the prepilin peptidase appear responsible for cleavage and methylation. Proteins with this N-terminal region include type IV pilins and other components of pilus biogenesis%2C competence proteins%2C and type II secretion proteins. Typically several proteins in a single operon have this N-terminal domain. The N-terminal cleavage and methylation site is described by PROSITE motif PS00409 as [KRHEQSTAG]-G-[FYLIVM]-[ST]-[LT]-[LIVP]-E-[LIVMFWSTAG](14). [Cell envelope%2C Surface structures%2C Protein fate%2C Protein and peptide secretion and trafficking] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-137%2C Eval:5.1e-09%2C score:49.4],MGA_1726
