sequence02	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	148907	149332	.	+	0	ID=MGA_1789;product=VOC family protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_011268094.1;translation=MSLSPFHLAIPVYDLAAARTFYGEVFGLAEGRSSAQWVDFDFYGHQLVIHEQPKTPSQESVHSNPVDGHDVPVPHFGIILEWVQWEALAERLKSFGTQFVIEPYIRFKGQVGEQATMFLFDPCGNALEFKAFKDMSQLFAK;locus_tag=LOCUS_17870;note=WP_011268094.1 VOC family protein (Pseudomonas) [pid:95.0%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:2.6e-76],Domain:cl14632:VOC vicinal oxygen chelate (VOC) family. Toxoflavin lyase (TflA) is metalloenzyme degrading  toxoflavin at the presence of  oxygen%2C Mn(II)%2C and dithiothreitol. TflA is structurally homologous to proteins of the vicinal oxygen chelate superfamily. The structure of TflA contains  fold that displays a rare rearrangement of the structural modules indicative of domain permutation. Moreover%2C unlike the 2-His-1-carboxylate facial triad commonly utilized by vicinal oxygen chelate dioxygenases and other dioxygen-activating non-heme Fe(II) enzymes%2C the metal center in TflA consists of a 1-His-2-carboxylate facial triad. Toxoflavin  is an azapteridine that is toxic to various plants%2C fungi%2C animals%2C and bacteria. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-141%2C Eval:5.3e-73%2C score:212.0],MGA_1789
