sequence02	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	236527	237501	.	+	0	ID=MGA_1871;product=decarboxylating 6-phosphogluconate dehydrogenase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_005766216.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_18690;gene=gnd;note=WP_005766216.1 decarboxylating 6-phosphogluconate dehydrogenase (Pseudomonas syringae group) [pid:92.9%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:4.1e-173],Domain:cl25951:NAD_binding_11 NAD-binding of NADP-dependent 3-hydroxyisobutyrate dehydrogenase. This family resembles a larger family (gnd) of bacterial and eukaryotic 6-phosphogluconate dehydrogenases but differs from it by a deep split in a UPGMA similarity clustering tree and the lack of a central region of about 140 residues. Among complete genomes%2C it is found is found in Bacillus subtilis and Mycobacterium tuberculosis%2C both of which also contain gnd%2C and in Aquifex aeolicus. The protein from Methylobacillus flagellatus KT has been characterized as a decarboxylating 6-phosphogluconate dehydrogenase as part of an unusual formaldehyde oxidation cycle. In some sequenced organisms members of this family are the sole 6-phosphogluconate dehydrogenase present and are probably active in the pentose phosphate cycle. [Energy metabolism%2C Pentose phosphate pathway] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-324%2C Eval:1.8e-157%2C score:439.9],MGA_1871
