sequence03	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	303806	304369	.	+	0	ID=MGA_2603;product=L%2CD-transpeptidase family protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_011266926.1;translation=MRWLLAFFCMSFLPLSQAAFTQTIVPKGSEQKIINNKVINTESIASKKIDKVLVLKSARQLQLISDGEALKTYRISLGKNPKGTKLQEGDQRTPEGFYWLDWRKPSNNYNLSMHISYPNITDSARARNEGVKPGSMIMIHGTPVDEEYPEWYFHTLDWTNGCIAMKNNDMREVWDLVKDGTMIEIRP;locus_tag=LOCUS_26000;note=WP_011266926.1 L%2CD-transpeptidase family protein (Pseudomonas syringae) [pid:93.6%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:6.5e-103],Domain:cl21614:YkuD L%2CD-transpeptidase catalytic domain. This family of proteins are found in a range of bacteria. It has been shown that this domain can act as an L%2CD-transpeptidase that gives rise to an alternative pathway for peptidoglycan cross-linking. This gives bacteria resistance to beta-lactam antibiotics that inhibit PBPs which usually carry out the cross-linking reaction. The conserved region contains a conserved histidine and cysteine%2C with the cysteine thought to be an active site residue. Several members of this family contain peptidoglycan binding domains. The molecular structure of YkuD protein shows this domain has a novel tertiary fold consisting of a beta-sandwich with two mixed sheets%2C one containing five strands and the other%2C six strands. The two beta-sheets form a cradle capped by an alpha-helix. This family was formerly called the ErfK/YbiS/YcfS/YnhG family%2C but is now named after the first protein of known structure. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:48-187%2C Eval:2.9e-48%2C score:156.4%2C C-term missing],MGA_2603
