sequence03	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	363157	363651	.	+	0	ID=MGA_2658;product=type VI secretion system tube protein Hcp;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_011267330.1;translation=MSFDAFMQVDGVEGESLDDAHKGWVELLSYHYDAVQSISNTASSSGGATAGGVTLGDFRVSKYIDRATPKLFELCCRGSHINKVTIRVHRASTEKFKYLDIVLEEVLISTVSGNGAEHAGLPVEMITLNYGRIKFEYSQQQRADGGNAGIVSGGWDRTANKPFA;locus_tag=LOCUS_26550;note=WP_011267330.1 type VI secretion system tube protein Hcp (Pseudomonas syringae) [pid:86.0%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:1.8e-78],Domain:cl01226:T6SS_HCP Type VI secretion system effector%2C Hcp. This family includes Hcp1 (hemolysin coregulated protein 1)%2C an exported%2C homohexameric ring-forming virulence protein from Pseudomonas aeruginosa. Hcp1 lacks a conventional signal sequence and is instead exported by means of the type VI secretion system%2C encoded by a pathogenicity cluster of a class previously designated IAHP (IcmF-associated homologous protein). Homologs of Hcp1%2C in this protein family%2C are found in various bacteria of which most but not all are known pathogens. Pathogens may have many multiple members of this family%2C with three to ten in Erwinia carotovora%2C Yersinia pestis%2C uropathogenic Escherichia coli%2C and the insect pathogen Photorhabdus luminescens. [Cellular processes%2C Pathogenesis] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-161%2C Eval:4.1e-33%2C score:112.4],MGA_2658
