sequence03	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	652753	654399	.	+	0	ID=MGA_2925;product=tetratricopeptide repeat protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_074907579.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_29220;note=WP_074907579.1 tetratricopeptide repeat protein (Pseudomonas) [pid:94.5%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:95.3%25%2C Eval:3.0e-300],Domain:cl26002:TPR_11 TPR repeat. The Tetratricopeptide repeat (TPR) typically contains 34 amino acids and is found in a variety of organisms including bacteria%2C cyanobacteria%2C yeast%2C fungi%2C plants%2C and humans. It is present in a variety of proteins including those involved in chaperone%2C cell-cycle%2C transcription%2C and protein transport complexes. The number of TPR motifs varies among proteins. Those containing 5-6 tandem repeats generate a right-handed helical structure with an amphipathic channel that is thought to accommodate an alpha-helix of a target protein. It has been proposed that TPR proteins preferentially interact with WD-40 repeat proteins%2C but in many instances several TPR-proteins seem to aggregate to multi-protein complexes. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:428-545%2C Eval:3.0e-07%2C score:49.0%2C N-term missing],MGA_2925
