sequence04	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	224767	225297	.	+	0	ID=MGA_3208;product=2-oxo-4-hydroxy-4-carboxy-5-ureidoimidazoline decarboxylase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_011104660.1;translation=MNALPHLKPSTLSRDAFVATFADIYEHSPWIAQQAFDQGAGPELDQLDTLHARMSDILLRATHEQQLALINAHPDLAGKAAVRGELTQASTDEQAGAGIHLCTPEEFQRFTELNEAYKARFGFPFIMAVKGSDRHRILAAFEQRIHHSPEAEFACALAEINKIALFRLQALQASQS;locus_tag=LOCUS_32040;gene=uraD;EC_number=4.1.1.97;note=WP_011104660.1 2-oxo-4-hydroxy-4-carboxy-5-ureidoimidazoline decarboxylase (Pseudomonas syringae group genomosp. 3) [pid:88.1%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:3.7e-86],Domain:cl01251:OHCU_decarbox OHCU decarboxylase. Previously thought to only proceed spontaneously%2C the decarboxylation of 2-oxo-4-hydroxy-4-carboxy--5-ureidoimidazoline (OHCU) has been recently been shown to be catalyzed by this enzyme in Mus musculus. Homologs of this enzyme are found adjacent to and fused with uricase in a number of prokaryotes and are represented by this model. This model is a separate (but related) clade from that represented by TIGR3164. This model places a second homolog in streptomyces species which (are not in the vicinity of other urate catabolism associated genes) below the trusted cutoff. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-171%2C Eval:3.0e-73%2C score:215.3],MGA_3208
sequence04	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	225324	226319	.	+	0	ID=MGA_3209;product=allantoicase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_011267251.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_32050;gene=alc;EC_number=3.5.3.4;note=WP_011267251.1 allantoicase (Pseudomonas syringae) [pid:97.3%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:6.2e-193],Domain:cl27253:Allantoicase Allantoicase repeat. Members of this family are the enzyme allantoicase (EC 3.5.3.4)%2C also called allantoate amidinohydrolase. This enzyme hydrolyzes allantoate to (S)-ureidoglycolate and urea%3B it can also degrade (R)-ureidoglycolate to glyoxylate and urea. Allantoinase (EC 3.5.2.5) hydrolyzes (S)-allantoin (a xanthine metabolite%2C via urate) to allantoate. Allantoate can then be degraded either by this enzyme%2C allantoicase%2C or by allantoate deiminase (EC 3.5.3.9). Members of the seed alignment for this model were taken from BRENDA. Proteins in this family contain two copies of the allantoicase repeat (pfam03561). A different but similarly named enzyme%2C allantoate amidohydrolase (EC 3.5.3.9)%2C simultaneously breaks down the urea to ammonia and carbon dioxide. [Purines%2C pyrimidines%2C nucleosides%2C and nucleotides%2C Other%2C Energy metabolism%2C Other] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:8-328%2C Eval:0.0e+00%2C score:519.3],MGA_3209
