sequence05	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	76615	77331	.	-	0	ID=MGA_3430;product=phosphonate C-P lyase system protein PhnL;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_011104086.1;translation=MTTLIEVRDLSKTFTLHQHNGVVLNVLRGLNFSVRSGECLVLSGQSGAGKSTLLRTLYGNYLPAAGSIRVQHERQMIELVGATPRQVLDVRRKTLGYVSQFLRVIPRVSSLDVLMEPALARGWSREQAHERAQLLLTRLNIPQRLWPLAPSTFSGGEQQRINIARAFMVPWPVLLLDEPTASLDDANRQVVLELVTEAKQAGAALIGIFHDRDARESVADRQLDMTPVALTAKELQQC;locus_tag=LOCUS_34240;gene=phnL;note=WP_011104086.1 phosphonate C-P lyase system protein PhnL (Pseudomonas syringae group genomosp. 3) [pid:94.5%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:9.0e-123],Domain:cl28181:AAA ATPases associated with a variety of cellular activities. Members of this family are ATP-binding cassette (ABC) proteins by homology%2C but belong to energy coupling factor (ECF) transport systems. The architecture in general is two ATPase subunits (or a double-length fusion protein)%2C a T component%2C and a substrate capture (S) component that is highly variable%2C and may be interchangeable in genomes with only one T component. This model identifies many but not examples of the downstream member of the pair of ECF ATPases in Firmicutes and Mollicutes. [Transport and binding proteins%2C Unknown substrate] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-229%2C Eval:4.5e-138%2C score:384.5],MGA_3430
