sequence05	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	78182	79069	.	-	0	ID=MGA_3432;product=alpha-D-ribose 1-methylphosphonate 5-phosphate C-P-lyase PhnJ;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_011267545.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_34260;note=WP_011267545.1 alpha-D-ribose 1-methylphosphonate 5-phosphate C-P-lyase PhnJ (Pseudomonas) [pid:95.3%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:2.1e-165],Domain:cl01457:PhnJ Phosphonate metabolism protein PhnJ. This family consists of several bacterial phosphonate metabolism (PhnJ) sequences. The exact role that PhnJ plays in phosphonate utilisation is unknown. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:5-292%2C Eval:0.0e+00%2C score:568.7],MGA_3432
sequence05	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	79066	80145	.	-	0	ID=MGA_3433;product=carbon-phosphorus lyase complex subunit PhnI;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_011267544.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_34270;note=WP_011267544.1 carbon-phosphorus lyase complex subunit PhnI (Pseudomonas syringae) [pid:93.9%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:5.0e-191],Domain:cl01456:PhnI Bacterial phosphonate metabolism protein (PhnI). This family consists of several Proteobacterial phosphonate metabolism protein (PhnI) sequences. Bacteria that use phosphonates as a phosphorus source must be able to break the stable carbon-phosphorus bond. In Escherichia coli phosphonates are broken down by a C-P lyase that has a broad substrate specificity. The genes for phosphonate uptake and degradation in E. coli are organised in an operon of 14 genes%2C named phnC to phnP. Three gene products (PhnC%2C PhnD and PhnE) comprise a binding protein-dependent phosphonate transporter%2C which also transports phosphate%2C phosphite%2C and certain phosphate esters such as phosphoserine%3B two gene products (PhnF and PhnO) may have a role in gene regulation%3B and nine gene products (PhnG%2C PhnH%2C PhnI%2C PhnJ%2C PhnK%2C PhnL%2C PhnM%2C PhnN%2C and PhnP) probably comprise a membrane-associated C-P lyase enzyme complex. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-349%2C Eval:0.0e+00%2C score:636.0],MGA_3433
