sequence05	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	182738	184063	.	+	0	ID=MGA_3549;product=deoxyguanosinetriphosphate triphosphohydrolase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_004408510.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_35430;note=WP_004408510.1 deoxyguanosinetriphosphate triphosphohydrolase (Pseudomonas) [pid:97.7%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:99.5%25%2C Eval:1.5e-256],Domain:cl26231:YdhJ HD superfamily phosphohydrolase [General function prediction only]. dGTP triphosphohydrolase (dgt) releases inorganic triphosphate%2C an unusual activity reaction product%2C from GTP. Its activity has been called limited to the Enterobacteriaceae%2C although homologous sequences are detected elsewhere. This finding casts doubt on whether the activity is shared in other species. In several of these other species%2C the homologous gene is found in an apparent operon with dnaG%2C the DNA primase gene. The enzyme from E. coli was shown to bind coopertatively to single stranded DNA. The biological role of dgt is unknown. [Purines%2C pyrimidines%2C nucleosides%2C and nucleotides%2C Nucleotide and nucleoside interconversions] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:3-440%2C Eval:6.7e-121%2C score:355.9],MGA_3549
