sequence07	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	16827	17033	.	+	0	ID=MGA_3805;product=TraR/DksA family transcriptional regulator;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_032665755.1;translation=MADDIDRATEQAQYLLDVALFKHRRIPTSLVSSQFCEDCDDPIPEPRRAAILGCETCIHCQSLREQRR;locus_tag=LOCUS_37970;note=WP_032665755.1 TraR/DksA family transcriptional regulator (Enterobacter kobei) [pid:50.8%25%2C q_cov:95.6%25%2C s_cov:88.9%25%2C Eval:7.9e-11],Domain:cl00755:zf-dskA_traR Prokaryotic dksA/traR C4-type zinc finger. Members of this predicted regulatory protein are found only in endospore-forming members of the Firmicutes group of bacteria%2C and in nearly every such species%3B Clostridium perfringens seems to be an exception. The member from Bacillus subtilis%2C the model system for the study of the sporulation program%2C has been designated both yteA and yzwB. Some (but not all) members of this family show a strong sequence match to Pfam family pfam01258 the C4-type zinc finger protein%2C DksA/TraR family%2C but only one of the four key Cys residues is conserved. All members of this protein family share an additional C-terminal domain. Smaller proteins from the proteobacteria with just the N-terminal domain%2C including DksA and DksA2 are RNA polymerase-binding regulatory proteins even if the Zn-binding site is not conserved. [Unknown function%2C General] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:3-68%2C Eval:1.6e-10%2C score:49.7%2C N-term missing],MGA_3805
