sequence08	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	97659	97850	.	-	0	ID=MGA_4032;product=CcoQ/FixQ family Cbb3-type cytochrome c oxidase assembly chaperone;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_004408120.1;translation=MDIGMIRGLGTLVVMVAFIGLMLWVFSPARKAEFDDATLLPFADDPDAIRKVEHTATDKEDRP;locus_tag=LOCUS_40230;note=WP_004408120.1 CcoQ/FixQ family Cbb3-type cytochrome c oxidase assembly chaperone (Pseudomonas) [pid:83.9%25%2C q_cov:98.4%25%2C s_cov:98.4%25%2C Eval:2.4e-23],Domain:cl00282:cbb3_Oxidase_CcoQ N/A. This family consists of several Cbb3-type cytochrome oxidase components (FixQ/CcoQ). FixQ is found in nitrogen fixing bacteria. Since nitrogen fixation is an energy-consuming process%2C effective symbioses depend on operation of a respiratory chain with a high affinity for O2%2C closely coupled to ATP production. This requirement is fulfilled by a special three-subunit terminal oxidase (cytochrome terminal oxidase cbb3)%2C which was first identified in Bradyrhizobium japonicum as the product of the fixNOQP operon. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-47%2C Eval:1.5e-08%2C score:43.1],MGA_4032
