sequence08	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	119192	119734	.	-	0	ID=MGA_4050;product=exonuclease domain-containing protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_003315164.1;translation=MPHWLVIDLEATTEEGGWPVAEMEVIEIGATLVNQDGRELDHFERFVRPVRRPLLTHFCRQLTHISQSNIDSAAPLTTVWPQFERWLSHHRARVLGWASWGDYDRQQLEEEWRHHQLDSALSSMPHVNLKQRFAQARQLQKPLGLNSALQLAGMQFTGQQHRALVDARNTARLLPLIMPN;locus_tag=LOCUS_40410;note=WP_003315164.1 exonuclease domain-containing protein (Pseudomonas) [pid:93.9%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:1.1e-99],Domain:cl10012:DnaQ_like_exo DnaQ-like (or DEDD) 3%26apos%3B-5%26apos%3B exonuclease domain superfamily. This is a highly divergent 3' exoribonuclease family. The proteins constitute a typical RNase fold%2C where the active site residues form a magnesium catalytic centre. The protein of the solved structure readily cleaves 3### overhangs in a time-dependent manner. It is similar to DEDD-type RNases and is an unusual ATP-binding protein that binds ATP and dATP. It forms a dimer in solution and both protomers in the asymmetric unit bind a magnesium ion through Asp-6 in UniProtKB:P9WJ73. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-179%2C Eval:1.6e-82%2C score:240.2],MGA_4050
