sequence08	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	138830	139375	.	+	0	ID=MGA_4072;product=acireductone dioxygenase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_011267284.1;translation=MSSLSVYHVSSPDTPNKVLTHLEDIASTLAEQGVAFDRWEAATHIAPGASQEEVINAYRTQIDRLMNERGYVTVDVISLNSDHPQKAELRAKFLEEHRHGEDEVRFFVAGRGLFTLHIGDYVYAVLCEKNDLISVPAGTSHWFDMGENPHFVAIRLFNNPEGWVANFTGEDIAGRFPRLED;locus_tag=LOCUS_40630;note=WP_011267284.1 acireductone dioxygenase (Pseudomonas) [pid:94.5%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:8.6e-97],COG:COG1791:Adi1 Acireductone dioxygenase (methionine salvage)%2C cupin superfamily [Category:E%2C Aligned:1-179%2C Eval:2.3e-83%2C score:241.6],MGA_4072
sequence08	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	139392	140075	.	+	0	ID=MGA_4073;product=acireductone synthase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_005766869.1;translation=MPIKAVLTDIEGTTSAVSFVFDVLFPFARTHLPEFVRKNADQPQVASQLEAVRVQSEEPDADVERVIAILLEWIAEDRKATPLKALQGMVWEQGYNAGQLKGHVYPDAVEALQHWHRQGYSLYVYSSGSIQAQQLIFGCSEAGDLSGLFSGYFDTTSGPKREVQSYRTIAAAMSQDAHEVLFLSDIVEELDAAKAAGMATCGLIRDGGTLVGHKNVASFALIDPATF;locus_tag=LOCUS_40640;gene=mtnC;EC_number=3.1.3.77;note=WP_005766869.1 acireductone synthase (Pseudomonas syringae group) [pid:85.9%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:3.6e-110],Domain:cl21460:HAD_like Haloacid Dehalogenase-like Hydrolases. This subfamily includes the uncharacterized Bacillus subtilis YhcW. It belongs to the beta-phosphoglucomutase-like family whose other members include Lactococcus lactis beta-PGM%2C a mutase which catalyzes the interconversion of beta-D-glucose 1-phosphate (G1P) and D-glucose 6-phosphate (G6P)%2C Saccharomyces cerevisiae phosphatases GPP1 and GPP2 that dephosphorylate DL-glycerol-3-phosphate and DOG1 and DOG2 that dephosphorylate 2-deoxyglucose-6-phosphate%2C and Escherichia coli 6-phosphogluconate phosphatase YieH. This family belongs to the haloacid dehalogenase-like (HAD) hydrolases%2C a large superfamily of diverse enzymes that catalyze carbon or phosphoryl group transfer reactions on a range of substrates%2C using an active site aspartate in nucleophilic catalysis. Members of this superfamily include 2-L-haloalkanoic acid dehalogenase%2C azetidine hydrolase%2C phosphonoacetaldehyde hydrolase%2C phosphoserine phosphatase%2C phosphomannomutase%2C P-type ATPases and many others. HAD hydrolases are found in all three kingdoms of life%2C and most genomes are predicted to contain multiple HAD-like proteins. Members possess a highly conserved alpha/beta core domain%2C and many also possess a small cap domain%2C the fold and function of which is variable. HAD hydrolases are sometimes referred to as belonging to the DDDD superfamily of phosphohydrolases. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:3-220%2C Eval:1.1e-109%2C score:311.8],MGA_4073
