sequence09	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	78290	78793	.	-	0	ID=MGA_4204;product=type VI secretion system tube protein Hcp;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_003318810.1;translation=MAFDAFIWIDGIAGESRDSAHQDWIEATAFNLAATQGVSRTASSSGGATVGRVYLSDFSIVKLVDSSTPKIFQACCAGQHLKKVILSLYRAGGEKQKYMEVTFEEVIISGVESGNLFDRKPSSFPEEVIRFDYAKVKMIYSQQSRESGLLIGQISAGWDQISNNTYA;locus_tag=LOCUS_41930;note=WP_003318810.1 type VI secretion system tube protein Hcp (Pseudomonas) [pid:47.7%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:1.4e-39],Domain:cl01226:T6SS_HCP Type VI secretion system effector%2C Hcp. This family includes Hcp1 (hemolysin coregulated protein 1)%2C an exported%2C homohexameric ring-forming virulence protein from Pseudomonas aeruginosa. Hcp1 lacks a conventional signal sequence and is instead exported by means of the type VI secretion system%2C encoded by a pathogenicity cluster of a class previously designated IAHP (IcmF-associated homologous protein). Homologs of Hcp1%2C in this protein family%2C are found in various bacteria of which most but not all are known pathogens. Pathogens may have many multiple members of this family%2C with three to ten in Erwinia carotovora%2C Yersinia pestis%2C uropathogenic Escherichia coli%2C and the insect pathogen Photorhabdus luminescens. [Cellular processes%2C Pathogenesis] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-159%2C Eval:1.1e-28%2C score:101.3],MGA_4204
