sequence10	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	49288	50481	.	-	0	ID=MGA_4353;product=TerD family protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_011266646.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_43390;note=WP_011266646.1 TerD family protein (Pseudomonas syringae) [pid:91.7%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:1.8e-208],Domain:cl18957:TerD_like Uncharacterized proteins involved in stress response%2C similar to tellurium resistance terD. The TerD domain is found in TerD family proteins that include the paralogous TerD%2C TerA%2C TerE%2C TerF and TerZ proteins It is found in a stress response operon with TerB and TerC. TerD has a maximum of two calcium-binding sites depending on the conservation of aspartates. It has various fusions to nuclease domains%2C RNA binding domains%2C ubiquitin related domains%2C and metal binding domains. The ter gene products lie at the centre of membrane-linked metal recognition complexes with regulatory ramifications encompassing phosphorylation-dependent signal transduction%2C RNA-dependent regulation%2C biosynthesis of nucleoside-like metabolites and DNA processing linked to novel pathways. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:195-397%2C Eval:9.8e-98%2C score:287.1],COG:COG2310:TerZ Stress response protein SCP2 [Category:T%2C Aligned:28-163%2C Eval:4.4e-28%2C score:106.3],MGA_4353
